To generate RDF individuals for the given information, we need to map each piece of data into a specific ontology class and provide appropriate properties with values. Here's how you can structure it:

### Model Family

```sparql
PREFIX arch: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto#>
PREFIX train: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/trainingonto#>

INSERT DATA {
  :MatterSim v1 a arch:model_family ;
    rdfs:label "MatterSim v1" .
}
```

### Model Variant

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX trainind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/trainingonto-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :mattersim_v1_5m a archind:model_variant ;
    rdfs:label "mattersim_v1_5m" .
}
```

### Model Architectures

```sparql
PREFIX arch: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet a arch:model_architecture ;
    rdfs:label "M3GNet" ;
    has_hidden_dimension 10 ;
    has_layer_count 2 .
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer a arch:model_architecture ;
    rdfs:label "Graphormer" ;
    has_hidden_dimension 10 ;
    has_layer_count 4 .
}
```

### Architecture Parameters

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX trainind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/trainingonto-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet rdfs:label "1820000"^^xsd:long ;
    has_hidden_dimension 10 ;
    has_layer_count 2 .
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer rdfs:label "182000000"^^xsd:long ;
    has_hidden_dimension 10 ;
    has_layer_count 4 .
}
```

### Training Dataset

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX dataind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/dataset-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet rdfs:label "17 million"^^xsd:long ;
    uses_dataset "S3 Data distribution";
    was_derived_from_dataset "MPF2021, MPtrj, Alexandria datasets".
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer rdfs:label "182M"^^xsd:long ;
    uses_dataset "S3 Data distribution";
    was_derived_from_dataset "MPF2021, MPtrj, Alexandria datasets".
}
```

### Parameter Number

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX trainind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/trainingonto-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet rdfs:label "4,549,142"^^xsd:long ;
    has_parameter_number 4549142 .
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer rdfs:label "182000000"^^xsd:long ;
    has_parameter_number 182000000 .
}
```

### RDF Individuals

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX dataind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/dataset-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet a archind:model_variant ;
    rdfs:label "mattersim_v1_5m" .
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer a archind:model_variant ;
    rdfs:label "mattersim_v1_5m" .
}
```

### RDF Graph

```sparql
PREFIX arch: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto#>
PREFIX train: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/trainingonto#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet a arch:model_architecture ;
    rdfs:label "M3GNet" ;
    has_hidden_dimension 10 ;
    has_layer_count 2 .
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer a arch:model_architecture ;
    rdfs:label "Graphormer" ;
    has_hidden_dimension 10 ;
    has_layer_count 4 .
}
```

### RDF Graph (for Parameter Number)

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX trainind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/trainingonto-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet rdfs:label "1820000"^^xsd:long ;
    has_parameter_number 4549142 .
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer rdfs:label "182000000"^^xsd:long ;
    has_parameter_number 182000000 .
}
```

### RDF Graph (for Training Dataset)

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX dataind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/dataset-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet rdfs:label "17 million"^^xsd:long ;
    uses_dataset "S3 Data distribution";
    was_derived_from_dataset "MPF2021, MPtrj, Alexandria datasets".
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer rdfs:label "182M"^^xsd:long ;
    uses_dataset "S3 Data distribution";
    was_derived_from_dataset "MPF2021, MPtrj, Alexandria datasets".
}
```

### RDF Graph (for Parameter Number)

```sparql
PREFIX archind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/architectureonto-individuals#>
PREFIX trainind: <https://k.loria.fr/ontologies/trainingonto-individuals#>

INSERT DATA {
  :M3GNet rdfs:label "4,549,142"^^xsd:long ;
    has_parameter_number 4549142 .
}

INSERT DATA {
  :Graphormer rdfs:label "182000000"^^xsd:long ;
    has_parameter_number 182000000 .
}
```

These SPARQL queries generate RDF individuals for the model family, variant, architectures, parameters, and datasets. The `rdfs:label` property is used to provide a human-readable label for each individual, while other properties are used to store specific details such as parameter counts or dataset information.